# PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE] Contents of this Part

## The overriding objective

## 1.1

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (1) These Rules are a procedural code with the overriding objective of enabling the court to deal with cases justly and at proportionate cost.

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (2) Dealing with a case justly and at proportionate cost includes, so far as is practicable –

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (a) ensuring that the parties are on an equal footing and can participate fully in proceedings, and that parties and witnesses can give their best evidence;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (b) saving expense;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (c) dealing with the case in ways which are proportionate –

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (i) to the amount of money involved;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (ii) to the importance of the case;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (iii) to the complexity of the issues; and

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (iv) to the financial position of each party;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (d) ensuring that it is dealt with expeditiously and fairly;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (e) allotting to it an appropriate share of the court’s resources, while taking into account the need to allot resources to other cases;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] f) promoting or using alternative dispute resolution; and

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.1] (g) enforcing compliance with rules, practice directions and orders.

## Application by the court of the overriding objective

## 1.2

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.2] The court must seek to give effect to the overriding objective when it –

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.2] (a) exercises any power given to it by the Rules; or

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.2] (b) interprets any rule subject to rules 76.2, 79.2 and 80.2, 82.2 and 88.2.

## Duty of the parties

## 1.3

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.3] The parties are required to help the court to further the overriding objective.

## Court’s duty to manage cases

## 1.4

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (1) The court must further the overriding objective by actively managing cases.

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (2) Active case management includes –

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (a) encouraging the parties to co-operate with each other in the conduct of the proceedings;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (b) identifying the issues at an early stage;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (c) deciding promptly which issues need full investigation and trial and accordingly disposing summarily of the others;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (d) deciding the order in which issues are to be resolved;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (e) ordering or encouraging the parties to use, and facilitating the use of, alternative dispute resolution;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (f) helping the parties to settle the whole or part of the case;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (g) fixing timetables or otherwise controlling the progress of the case;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (h) considering whether the likely benefits of taking a particular step justify the cost of taking it;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (i) dealing with as many aspects of the case as it can on the same occasion;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (j) dealing with the case without the parties needing to attend at court;

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (k) making use of technology; and

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.4] (l) giving directions to ensure that the trial of a case proceeds quickly and efficiently.

## The Welsh language

## 1.5

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.5] (1) Nothing in the overriding objective undermines the principles provided by the Welsh Language (Wales) Measure 2011(3) that the Welsh language has official status in Wales or by the Welsh Language Act 1993(4) that in any legal proceedings in Wales the Welsh language may be used by any person who desires to use it.

[PART 1 – OVERRIDING OBJECTIVE > 1.5] (2) The parties are required to assist the court to put into effect the principles set out in paragraph (1)

## Participation of vulnerable parties or witnesses

## 1.6

# Practice Direction 1A makes provision for how the court is to give effect to the overriding objective in relation to vulnerable parties or witnesses.
